      "intent": "rules_qa",
      "stop_reason": "completed",
      "answer": "The Ready action lets you prepare to take a specific action in response to a defined trigger condition before your next turn begins. When you take the Ready action, you choose what circumstance will trigger your Reaction (e.g., 'If the cultist steps on the trapdoor, I'll pull the lever that opens it') and the action you'll take when that trigger occurs. You can then take your Reaction right after the trigger finishes or choose to ignore it. If you Ready a spell, you cast it as normal but hold its energy until the trigger occurs, which requires Concentration that you can maintain up to the star",
